TTING THE EVENING: run --scope-items 40 --build-only on padme first, convert doudou's rate to padme's from it, then confirm 200 or fall back to 150. PAIRING CHECK AFTER THE FACT: the writer runs at temperature 0, so the same sample yields the same questions -- diff the two arms' work-dir questions.jsonl, and if they differ the arms are unpaired and the comparison is void
2026-09-07T04:13Z claude corrected the implementation after two of this repo's own guards fired, and the correction is better than what it replaced. check_models (bench/check_models.py, the sixth guard: one model name, one place) refused the first draft twice -- first for writing the input template 'passage: ' as a literal, then for naming the repository Xenova/multilingual-e5-small in a driver. Both were right. SO THE TEMPLATE AND THE REVISION NOW COME FROM bench/models.json, resolved by registry_record() on registry id, then hf_repo, then upstream_repo (a registry id carries no slash, so the namespaces cannot collide): identity.embedder.registry names the record, its status, its upstream repo, its declared pooling and its languages; prefixes.expected is the record's input_template with expected_from saying which record it came from; revision.declared is the record's hf_revision with pinned_at_load false, because the target passes no revision to the pipeline -- so the declaration is recorded as a declaration and the weights digest stays the measurement of what this run actually held. A repository the registry does not declare yields expected null with expected_from saying UNRESOLVED, never 'no markers': the two are different facts and only one of them is a property of the model. The E5 id-inference regex that the first draft copied out of embeddings.ts is gone with it -- the registry knows which models want the markers, so nothing here duplicates the target's tables. ADDED WITH IT: pooling_disagrees_with_registry, fired when the stamp's pooling and bench/models.json disagree, which is the silent retrieval loss that ticket 0421 measured at 10-27% of MRR. The second guard, test_index_driver_roster_closure, refused the new read of meta.embedderId against a pinned table set of {items}; its EXCUSED entry for bench/generator/run.py now pins {items, meta} and its reason names the second read and why it is still not a figure. TESTS now ten, all ten red against HEAD's run.py, all green after; make check-fast 1198 passed and make lint clean
--- body ---
## Context

The library-level bench (ticket 0719, merged in PR #406) put 100 questions
from the author's own library to the reviewed zoteus build and found
cross-lingual retrieval near zero, in every retrieval mode:

| lane | n | win | near-win | miss |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| en→en | 59 | 20 | 35 | 4 |
| vi→vi | 8 | 1 | 5 | 2 |
| fr→en | 12 | 1 | 4 | 7 |
| vi→en | 10 | 0 | 0 | 10 |

Keyword found the work in 3 of 30 cross-lingual cases, vectors in 9, hybrid
in 9, so the failure is not a mode effect. Same-language retrieval is healthy
at 0,76 reciprocal rank for English.

**What the run did not record is which model produced those vectors.** The
run identity says the embedder is local and active; it does not name it. That
single fact decides what the finding means, and the two readings are opposite:

- If the build loaded a **multilingual** embedder, this is a failure of a
  requirement the project has ratified, and R29 is broken at library level in
  the direction ruling 2 of 2026-09-06 added, a Vietnamese query against
  English content.
- If the build loaded the **English-only incumbent** (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2`, the
  model the feasibility runs used), then the numbers are the expected
  behaviour of a monolingual model and say nothing about R29. What they would
  then be evidence for is a shipped default that cannot keep R7 or R29 at all.

Reporting either reading before the model is named would be a verdict dressed
as a finding (`rules/workflow.md` § Diagnosis discipline).

## Actions

1. Read, from the reviewed build's own source and configuration rather than
   from documentation, which model the default path loads: the registry entry,
   the resolved model id, its dtype and pooling.
2. Record the model id, revision and pooling in the bench's `run` block, so no
   future run can be read without it. SPEC.md §5.2.10 already requires a run
   identity; this is the field it is missing.
3. Re-run the cross-lingual lanes and state the verdict against R29 explicitly,
   naming the model.
4. If the default is monolingual, say so where a reader of the requirement
   will meet it, and open the question of what the shipped default should be.

## Exit criteria
- [x] the embedder actually loaded by the default path is named, from source
      (and, since 2026-09-07, measured: the recorded arm's own index stamps
      `local:Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`)
- [x] the bench's run identity carries model id, revision, dtype and pooling
      (`identity.embedder` in `bench/generator/run.py`; the target pins no
      revision, so the weights are identified by digest and the absence of a
      pin is stated rather than papered over)
- [ ] the cross-lingual lanes re-run and their verdict against R29 stated with
      the model named — blocked: Zotero is not running on padme, and doudou's
      is out of bounds
